The bug occurs because the code incorrectly references `sourceNode` instead of `source.currentNode`, which can lead to accessing outdated or incorrect node data during the reclaim process. This misreference can cause improper handling of child nodes, affecting the reclaim logic and potentially leading to unexpected behavior in the tree structure.

